    <item>
      <title>From Storm to Scare Story: How The Guardian Wrongly Claimed Climate Change Caused a ‘Climate Breakdown’</title>
      <link>https://wattsupwiththat.com/2025/12/04/from-storm-to-scare-story-how-the-guardian-wrongly-claimed-climate-change-caused-a-climate-breakdown/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=from-storm-to-scare-story-how-the-guardian-wrongly-claimed-climate-change-caused-a-climate-breakdown</link>
      <description>By implying that a heartbreaking family tragedy is proof of global climate collapse, The Guardian irresponsibly misleads its readers, substituting emotional persuasion and advocacy with scientific rigor. Readers deserve factual reporting complete with historical context and data, rather than a false narrative that treats every intense weather event as evidence of a “climate breakdown.”</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://wattsupwiththat.com/2025/12/04/from-storm-to-scare-story-how-the-guardian-wrongly-claimed-climate-change-caused-a-climate-breakdown/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=from-storm-to-scare-story-how-the-guardian-wrongly-claimed-climate-change-caused-a-climate-breakdown</guid>
